I was the one who wrote and posted it. Meanwhile, it has been placed on
the good old ftp site at:
	altair.krl.caltech.edu
as
	/pub/nethack/bw/nhdecode.c

Last time I checked, the site manager had not yet changed the read
permissions to "all", though, so it may take a while before you can
actually upload it. Anyway, you can also write a program like this
yourself. The encoding process was very simple: do an XOR 1 on the
first character of a line, XOR 2 on the second, XOR 4 on the third,
XOR 8 on the fourth, and XOR 16 on the fifth. Repeat for characters
6-10. Repeat for characters 11-15. Repeat. Repeat. Get the trick?

